menu "GM Synth bring-up"

config GM_SYNTH_PCM_ARENA_BYTES
    int "PCM PSRAM arena size (bytes)"
    range 1048576 6291456
    default 4194304
    help
        Initial M0/M3 PCM residency arena reserved from external PSRAM.
        The default is intentionally conservative (4 MiB) on an 8 MiB N16R8
        target so later Voice/FX/index/system allocations retain headroom.
        This is a bring-up value, not the final production memory budget.

config GM_SYNTH_STORAGE_BENCHMARK_ENABLE
    bool "Run SF2 VFS -> PSRAM storage benchmark at boot"
    default n
    help
        Bring-up only. When enabled, app_main opens an already-mounted VFS path,
        locates the SoundFont smpl payload, and benchmarks sequential reads into
        the PCM PSRAM arena using 4/8/16/32/64 KiB chunks. This option does not
        mount a filesystem and must remain disabled for normal runtime builds.

if GM_SYNTH_STORAGE_BENCHMARK_ENABLE

config GM_SYNTH_STORAGE_BENCHMARK_PATH
    string "Mounted SF2 path used by storage benchmark"
    default "/sf2/test.sf2"
    help
        Path visible through ESP-IDF VFS. Board-specific code must mount the
        corresponding FAT/LittleFS/SD filesystem before this benchmark runs.

config GM_SYNTH_STORAGE_BENCHMARK_BYTES
    int "Maximum smpl bytes read per benchmark pass"
    range 65536 4194304
    default 4194304
    help
        Each chunk-size pass reads up to this many bytes from the contiguous SF2
        smpl payload directly into the caller-owned PSRAM arena. The runtime also
        clamps this value to the actual smpl payload and arena capacity.

endif

endmenu
